cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or adapt this code, please cite this repository."
type: software
title: "orbit-complexity: Lean verification of Orbit structures and complexity in Schubert and Richardson Varieties"
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 formalization of Y. Gao and R. Hodges, "Orbit structures and
  complexity in Schubert and Richardson Varieties": the torus complexity of a
  Richardson variety is the length difference minus the algebraic dimension of
  its Bruhat interval, which is also the largest toric subinterval drop
  (Theorem 1.2), and of a Schubert variety the length minus the support
  (Corollary 1.3); the torus weights on each Deodhar component (Theorem 1.4);
  a codimension-preserving correspondence between Levi-Borel orbits of a
  Schubert cell and torus orbits of a smaller cell (Theorem 1.5); and the
  Levi complexity of a Schubert variety stable under a Levi subgroup
  (Theorem 1.6), together with every other statement of the paper. The
  accompanying libraries develop flag varieties, reductive groups and their
  root data, Bruhat intervals, algebraic group actions with Rosenlicht's
  theorem, Frobenius splitting, and the geometry of Schubert and Richardson
  varieties, including their normality.
authors:
  - family-names: Hodges
    given-names: Reuven
version: "1.0.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/rhodges-math/orbit-complexity"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - Lean 4
  - Mathlib
  - formalization
  - Schubert varieties
  - Richardson varieties
  - complexity of group actions
  - Bruhat interval polytopes
  - Levi subgroups
